:0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### What version of React Router are you using?\r\n\r\nv6.0.1\r\n\r\n### Steps to Reproduce\r\n\r\n**App.js**\r\n```js\r\nimport React from 'react'\r\nimport { BrowserRouter, Route, Routes, useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom'\r\n\r\nfunction App () {\r\n   const navigate = useNavigate()\r\n\r\n   return (\r\n      <Routes>\r\n         <Route path=\"/\" element={<Index navigate={navigate} />} />\r\n         <Route path=\"/next\" element={<Next navigate={navigate}/>} />\r\n      </Routes>\r\n   )\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport default () => (\r\n   <BrowserRouter>\r\n      <App />\r\n   </BrowserRouter>\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Index.js**\r\n```js\r\nclass Index extends Component {\r\n\r\n   componentDidMount () {\r\n      const { navigate } = this.props\r\n      ...\r\n      if (!params.myName) {\r\n         // redirect navigate\r\n         navigate('/next')\r\n      }\r\n   }\r\n\r\n   render () {\r\n      return <div>Index Page!</div>\r\n   }\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport default Index\r\n```\r\n\r\n> When executing `navigate('/next')` function in Index.js Component, it does not work.\r\n> It works if you use the `setTimeout` function as shown below.\r\n```js\r\nsetTimeout(() => {\r\n   navigate('/next')\r\n}, 1)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Expected Behavior\r\n\r\nWhen the navigate('/next') function is executed, it should navigate to the \"/next\" page.\r\n\r\n### Actual Behavior\r\n\r\nIt doesn't \bwork anything.","closed_by":{"login":"timdorr","id":17882,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17882?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timdorr","html_url":"https://github.com/timdorr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timdorr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timdorr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timdorr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url"